WEBVTT

00:00:00.213 --> 00:00:04.695
Open Advanced Automation, Scripts, Change Virtual Switch MTU

00:00:04.736 --> 00:00:08.983
as an administrator. This standalone action targets the default V S

00:00:09.003 --> 00:00:12.487
zero, or B R zero, on the supported healthy cluster.

00:00:12.597 --> 00:00:16.908
Unlike the PE-direct uplink wizard, this workflow uses the supported

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.127
Prism Central networking API.

00:00:19.296 --> 00:00:21.559
Prism Central trust remains required.

00:00:21.728 --> 00:00:26.252
PE certificate verification is optional per operation, with an audited reason

00:00:26.293 --> 00:00:30.592
for an exception. Review the intended cluster UUID, saved

00:00:30.612 --> 00:00:34.731
credentials, active-backup bond and physical network support for jumbo

00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:39.011
frames. Confirm maintenance capacity and out-of-band access.

00:00:39.341 --> 00:00:43.716
The reviewed change raises the physical uplink MTU from fifteen hundred to

00:00:43.736 --> 00:00:47.109
nine thousand while preserving the existing bond and uplinks.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:51.451
Run read-only preflight and inspect every host and physical uplink.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.556
Missing or inconsistent readback blocks application.

00:00:54.768 --> 00:00:59.057
Have another administrator approve the exact plan, then use the cluster-bound

00:00:59.077 --> 00:01:02.440
confirmation only in a separately validated environment.

00:01:02.598 --> 00:01:06.270
Packaged appliances enable reviewed live application by default;

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.576
an explicit host override can retain planning mode.

00:01:09.766 --> 00:01:12.599
This demonstration performs no MTU changes.

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:17.006
Follow the Prism task and per-host readback in Jobs and Queue.

00:01:17.159 --> 00:01:21.747
Keep controller virtual machine interface MTU at fifteen hundred as documented.

00:01:21.937 --> 00:01:25.534
Verify end-to-end traffic on the intended VLANs separately.

00:01:25.713 --> 00:01:29.874
A successful task alone does not prove that the physical switching path carries

00:01:29.894 --> 00:01:33.821
jumbo frames correctly. Reconcile the original Prism task

00:01:33.862 --> 00:01:38.452
first. Enter the settled change job identifier and review the recorded original

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:41.354
MTU against current identity and settings.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.419
Request fresh rollback approval and confirmation.

00:01:44.624 --> 00:01:48.956
If telemetry is unavailable, use the site console recovery procedure;

00:01:49.061 --> 00:01:52.680
the workflow does not automatically reverse an uncertain write.
